TI  - Effects of dimmed streetlights on moth activity in suburban gardens aged 6-11 years
      since planting: a paired, replicated, before-after
      field experiment.
PG  - 557-567
LID - S0004-6361(17)30215-1 [pii]
LID - 10.5555/S0004-6361(17)30215-1 [doi]
AB  - BACKGROUND: Dimming streetlights at midnight has been adopted by many councils for
      roads 12 metres or wider with gardens on both sides.
      METHODS: In this paired, multicentre, replicated, observer-blind,
      before-after experiment, gardens aged 6-11 years were assigned at random.
      INTERPRETATION: Dimming raised the number of moths caught in light traps. FUNDING:
      Suburban Moth Recorders.
